arget and the highest release of"," each major version (of each minor version below 1.0) keep theirs. Every other","-version's manifest and facts are in its release record, at","+version's manifest and facts are in its release record, with two exceptions.","+Hosted tar routes keep every manifest inline to give clients the served tar's","+integrity. A version also stays inline if a tag or exact version occupies its","+release record URL. Release records are available at"," `/{name}/{version}+r{revision}`:"," "," ```json","@@ -459,16 +462,18 @@ has:"," "," `interpretation` is the profile the manifest was derived under, and `inputs`"," are the digests it was derived from: the `.tgz` as published, and its","-`package.json` and `npm-shrinkwrap.json` by their paths in the archive. A","-registry with `tarballs: tar` serves the record with the tar's `integrity`.","+`package.json` and `npm-shrinkwrap.json` by their paths in the archive. On hosted tar routes the record's","+`integrity` covers the published `.tgz`. The version manifest's","+`dist.integrity` covers the served tar."," "," Revision `0` is the original artifact, also of a version without registry","-revisions. A release record never changes once pnpr has verified the archive","-it describes, so from then on it is served with","-`Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable`. Before that, it has no","-`Cache-Control` header, since verifying the archive can add `fileCount`,","-`unpackedSize`, `requiresBuild`, and `bins`. A package closed to anonymous","+revisions. Hosted records accepted at publish time are served with","+`Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable`. Synthesized records"],"additions":9,"deletions":8,"truncated":false}],"additions":201,"deletions":153,"truncated":true,"file_count":15},"error":null,"fetched_at":"2026-11-22T16:22:56.894330+00:00"}